      "math_academy_id": "q-225003",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(15)$ given below, compute $P(X=9).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0028\\,$ | $\\,0.0076\\,$ | $\\,0.0180\\,$ | $\\,0.0374\\,$ | $\\,0.0699\\,$ | $\\,0.1185\\,$ | $\\,0.1848\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=9)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(9) & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,9\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,8\\})+P(X=9) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 8)+P(X=9) \\\\  & =F(8)+P(X=9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=9) & =F(9)-F(8) \\\\  & =0.0699-0.0374 \\\\  & =0.0325.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
